---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../../assets/Banner_KivaKamp.png";
import PageSection from "../../components/PageSection.astro";
import SectionBreakLeaf from "../../components/SectionBreakLeaf.astro";

import kivakamp1 from "../../assets/kivakamp1.png";
import kivakamp2 from "../../assets/kivakamp2.png";
import kivakamp3 from "../../assets/kivakamp3.png";

import FramedImage from "../../components/FramedImage.astro";
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={null} heroSrc={heroImage.src}>
    <PageSection headingLevel={2} contentWidth="narrow">
        <div class="stack-lg">
            <p>
                Kiva Kamps was launched as a celebration of Kiva's values,
                philosophy and pedagogy: blending elements of learning through
                play with activities of daily living. Stepping away from the
                academic year, Kiva Kamps is an extension of Kiva's teaching and
                learning experience in which both internal and external
                facilitators curate a dedicated program to encourage exploration
                and discovery in different fields, giving students the
                opportunity to find their pathway, while picking up some new
                skills.
            </p>
        </div>
    </PageSection>
    <PageSection title="WINTER KAMPS" headingLevel={2} contentWidth="narrow">
        <div class="stack-lg">
            <FramedImage imgSrc={kivakamp1.src} frameColor="yellow" />
            <p>
                The first iteration of Kiva Kamp happened in <strong>Winter
                    2024</strong> with an exclusive focus on
                <strong>Gymnastics</strong>, aiming to push students towards
                building strength, flexibility and confidence while 'playing'.
                Under the supervision of a trained facilitator, each child was
                supported well and en-couraged to go beyond their fears and
                reservations.
            </p>
        </div>
    </PageSection>

    <SectionBreakLeaf />

    <PageSection
        title="Welcoming Ramzan"
        headingLevel={2}
        contentWidth="narrow"
    >
        <div class="stack-lg">
            <FramedImage imgSrc={kivakamp2.src} frameColor="purple" />
            <p>
                To honour Ramzan, Kiva Kamp hosted a <strong>3-day Kamp
                    weekend</strong> welcoming the holy month with curated
                activities and sessions around kindness, gratitude and
                reflection. When children explore meaningful traditions through
                play, creativity and connection, their curiosity deepens and so
                does their understanding of the world around them.
            </p>

            <p>
                The spirit of Ramzan isn't just taught, it's felt, shared and
                experienced together as a community. In this Kamp weekend, we
                had activities such as '<strong>Chef it Up</strong>' in which
                our students made snacks for iftar, '<strong>Story time</strong>'
                centered around stories of different prophets in Islam,
                '<strong>Screen Printing</strong>' in which our students created
                Eid Mubarak prints, and '<strong>Paper Crafts</strong>'
                consisted of creating lanterns.
            </p>
        </div>
    </PageSection>

    <SectionBreakLeaf />

    <PageSection title="SUMMERS AT KIVA" headingLevel={2} contentWidth="narrow">
        <div class="stack-lg">
            <FramedImage imgSrc={kivakamp3.src} frameColor="purple" />
            <p>
                In 2025, Kiva Kamps hosted 'Summers at Kiva' - a month-long
                summer camp featuring 8 curated modules between the two
                different age groups. Open to external students, Summers at Kiva
                had a turnout of 62 students who participated in activities like
                <strong>Chef it Up, Storyweavers, Art & Craft, STEM and
                    Robotics, Woodworks, Digital Art, Gymnastics, Teddy Tennis,
                    and Futsal</strong>.
            </p>

            <p>
                With a holistic and varied summer program, there was plenty of
                opportunity to dabble in different activities and create things
                out of play. From learning to make sweet little treats to
                building a sturdy beach chair and robot, our Kampers took part
                in new activities with full gusto. They challenged themselves
                with each hurdle whether it be in sports or art, and learned to
                step out of their comfort zone with every little step forward.
            </p>
        </div>
    </PageSection>

    <SectionBreakLeaf />
</BaseLayout>
